<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="2CO" style="id">2 CORINTHIANS</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2CO 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 1:1"/>
    Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus through God’s sovereign will, along with Timothy our brother, 
    <verse eid="2CO 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">To God’s church located in Corinth, together with all the saints throughout the entire region of Achaia:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 1:2"/>
    May you experience grace and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Ascription of Blessedness to God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 1:3"/>
    Praise belongs to the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father characterised by mercies and the God who provides every comfort,
    <verse eid="2CO 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 1:4"/>
    the One who consoles us in every affliction we experience, enabling us to console those facing any kind of trouble, using the same comfort God Himself provides to us.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 1:5"/>
    Just as Christ’s sufferings abound in our lives, so through Christ our comfort also abounds.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 1:6"/>
    When we endure hardship, it benefits your comfort and salvation; when we receive comfort, it benefits your comfort, which proves effective as you patiently endure the same sufferings we also face.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 1:7"/>
    Our confident expectation for you remains firm, because we understand that just as you participate in our sufferings, so you also participate in our comfort.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Divine Rescue</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 1:8"/>
    We do not want you uninformed, brothers and sisters, about the severe affliction that came upon us in Asia—we were crushed by burdens far exceeding our strength, so much so that we lost all hope of surviving.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 1:9"/>
    In fact, we felt the sentence of death already passed within ourselves, so that we would rely not on our own resources, but on God, who raises the dead,
    <verse eid="2CO 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 1:10"/>
    who rescued us from such deadly peril, and who continues rescuing us, in whom we have placed our confident hope that He will rescue us again,
    <verse eid="2CO 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 1:11"/>
    as you also join in helping us through your prayers, so that many people may give thanks on our behalf for the gracious favour bestowed on us in answer to many prayers.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Integrity of Paul and Others</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 1:12"/>
    This is our reason for confidence: Our conscience testifies that we have conducted ourselves in the world, and especially towards you, with sincerity and purity from God—not with earthly wisdom but with God’s grace.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 1:13"/>
    We write you nothing beyond what you can read and understand, and I hope you will understand completely,
    <verse eid="2CO 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 1:14"/>
    just as you have already understood us in part—that we are your reason for pride, just as you are ours, on the day of our Lord Jesus.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Paul’s Change of Plans</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 1:15"/>
    With this confidence, I originally planned to visit you, so that you might receive a second experience of blessing,
    <verse eid="2CO 1:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 1:16"/>
    and to pass through your area on my way to Macedonia, then return from Macedonia to you, and have you send me on towards Judea.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 1:17"/>
    When I made these plans, did I act with fickleness? Or do I make plans according to human standards, saying “Yes, yes” and “No, no” at the same time?
    <verse eid="2CO 1:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 1:18"/>
    As surely as God is faithful, our message to you has not been “Yes” and “No.”
    <verse eid="2CO 1:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="2CO 1:19"/>
    For the Son of God, Jesus Christ, whom we proclaimed among you—Silvanus, Timothy, and I—was not “Yes” and “No,” but in Him it has always been “Yes.”
    <verse eid="2CO 1:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="2CO 1:20"/>
    For all of God’s promises find their “Yes” in Him; therefore, through Him we also say “Amen” to the glory of God through us.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="2CO 1:21"/>
    Now the One who firmly establishes us with you in Christ and who anointed us is God,
    <verse eid="2CO 1:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="2CO 1:22"/>
    who also sealed us and placed the down payment of the Spirit in our hearts.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="2CO 1:23"/>
    I call upon God as my witness—it was to spare you that I did not return to Corinth.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="2CO 1:24"/>
    Not that we lord it over your faith, but we work alongside you for your joy, for you stand firm in your faith.
    <verse eid="2CO 1:24"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="2CO 2"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 2:1"/>
    Yet I resolved this matter within myself: for your benefit, I chose not to make another visit that would bring renewed sorrow.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 2:2"/>
    For if I am the cause of your pain, who then would be the source of my encouragement, except those whom I have saddened?
    <verse eid="2CO 2:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 2:3"/>
    That is why I wrote as I did, so that when I eventually came, I would not be distressed by those who should have been my joy. I had confidence in all of you that my joy is inseparably tied to the joy of you all.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 2:4"/>
    For I wrote to you out of deep affliction and inner anguish, with many tears, not with the intention of causing you pain, but so that you might fully understand the depth of my love for you.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Reaffirming Love for the Offender</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 2:5"/>
    Now if someone has caused sorrow, he has not brought sorrow upon me alone, but in part—and I say this gently—upon all of you.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 2:6"/>
    The corrective discipline imposed by the majority is sufficient for such a person.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 2:7"/>
    Therefore, instead of continuing in severity, you should forgive him and comfort him, so that he is not overwhelmed and crushed by excessive sorrow.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 2:8"/>
    For this reason, I urge you to reaffirm your love towards him in a tangible way.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 2:9"/>
    Indeed, this was one purpose of my earlier writing: to test the genuineness of your character and to see whether you would demonstrate obedience in all matters.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 2:10"/>
    Now whoever you forgive, I also forgive. For whatever I have forgiven, if there was anything to forgive, I did so for your sake, standing before Christ.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 2:11"/>
    This was so that Satan would not gain an advantage over us, for we are well aware of his schemes and intentions.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 2:12"/>
    Now when I came to Troas for the proclamation of the gospel of Christ, even though an opportunity for ministry had been opened to me by the Lord,
    <verse eid="2CO 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 2:13"/>
    my spirit found no rest because I did not find Titus, my brother. Therefore, I said farewell to them and went on into Macedonia.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Triumphal Procession in Christ and the New Covenant Ministers</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 2:14"/>
    But thanks be to God, who continually leads us as captives in His victorious procession in Christ, and who makes known through us the aroma of the knowledge of Him everywhere.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 2:15"/>
    For we are, to God, the pleasing aroma of Christ among both those who are being saved and those who are perishing.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 2:16"/>
    To the one group, we are a scent that issues from death and leads to death; to the other, a scent that issues from life and leads to life. And who is adequate for such a calling?
    <verse eid="2CO 2:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 2:17"/>
    For we are not like the many who treat the word of God as a commodity for profit. Rather, we speak with sincerity, as those sent from God, speaking before God in union with Christ.
    <verse eid="2CO 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="2CO 3"/>
  <para style="s1">The New Covenant Ministry of the Spirit/Righteousness</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 3:1"/>
    Are we once again trying to recommend ourselves to you? Or do we require, as some do, letters of endorsement addressed to you or written on our behalf by you?
    <verse eid="2CO 3:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 3:2"/>
    You yourselves are our letter, engraved upon our hearts, publicly recognised and read by all people,
    <verse eid="2CO 3:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 3:3"/>
    clearly demonstrating that you are a letter belonging to Christ, produced through our ministry, written not with ink but with the Spirit of the living God, not on tablets of stone but on tablets that are human hearts.
    <verse eid="2CO 3:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 3:4"/>
    Such confidence we possess through Christ as we stand before God.
    <verse eid="2CO 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 3:5"/>
    It is not that we are adequate in ourselves to claim anything as originating from our own ability, but our adequacy comes from God,
    <verse eid="2CO 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 3:6"/>
    who has made us fully capable to serve as ministers of a new covenant, not characterised by written code but by the Spirit. For the written code brings death, but the Spirit imparts life.
    <verse eid="2CO 3:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 3:7"/>
    Now if the ministry that brought death, carved in letters on stone, came with glory, so that the sons of Israel could not fix their eyes on the face of Moses because of the radiance of his face—a radiance that was fading away—
    <verse eid="2CO 3:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 3:8"/>
    how much greater will the glory be of the ministry that belongs to the Spirit?
    <verse eid="2CO 3:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 3:9"/>
    For if the ministry that resulted in condemnation possessed glory, far more does the ministry that brings righteousness overflow with glory.
    <verse eid="2CO 3:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 3:10"/>
    Indeed, what once had glory has come to have no glory by comparison, because of the surpassing glory that now eclipses it.
    <verse eid="2CO 3:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 3:11"/>
    For if what was temporary came with glory, how much more does what is permanent remain in glory?
    <verse eid="2CO 3:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 3:12"/>
    Therefore, since we have such a hope, we speak with great boldness,
    <verse eid="2CO 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 3:13"/>
    and not as Moses did, who placed a veil over his face so that the sons of Israel would not gaze intently at the outcome of what was passing away.
    <verse eid="2CO 3:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 3:14"/>
    But their minds were hardened. For to this very day, the same veil remains unlifted when the old covenant is read, because it is only in Christ that it is removed.
    <verse eid="2CO 3:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 3:15"/>
    Indeed, to this day, whenever Moses is read, a veil lies over their heart;
    <verse eid="2CO 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 3:16"/>
    but whenever a person turns to the Lord, the veil is taken away.
    <verse eid="2CO 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 3:17"/>
    Now the Lord is the Spirit, and where the Spirit of the Lord is present, there is freedom.
    <verse eid="2CO 3:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 3:18"/>
    And we all, with faces uncovered, reflecting the glory of the Lord as in a mirror, are continually being transformed into the same image, moving from one degree of glory to another, just as this transformation comes from the Lord, who is the Spirit.
    <verse eid="2CO 3:18"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="2CO 4"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 4:1"/>
    For this reason, since we have received this ministry by the mercy of God, we do not become discouraged.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 4:2"/>
    Instead, we have rejected secret and shameful practices. We do not conduct ourselves with deceit, nor do we distort the word of God. Rather, by openly setting forth the truth, we commend ourselves to every man’s conscience in the sight of God.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 4:3"/>
    And even if our gospel is veiled, it is veiled only to those who are perishing.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 4:4"/>
    In their case, the god of this age has blinded the minds of unbelievers, so that they cannot see the light of the gospel that displays the glory of Christ, who is the visible image of God.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 4:5"/>
    For we do not proclaim ourselves, but Jesus Christ as Lord, and ourselves as your servants for the sake of Jesus.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 4:6"/>
    For God, who said, “Light shall shine out of darkness,”* is the One who has shone in our hearts, granting us the light of the knowledge of the glory of God as it is revealed in the face of Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Divine Treasure in Earthen Vessels</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 4:7"/>
    But we possess this priceless treasure in fragile, earthly containers, so that the extraordinary greatness of the power may be clearly seen as coming from God and not from us.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 4:8"/>
    We are pressed on every side, yet not crushed; confused, yet not driven to despair;
    <verse eid="2CO 4:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 4:9"/>
    persecuted, yet not abandoned; struck down, yet not destroyed.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 4:10"/>
    We continually carry in our bodies the dying of Jesus, so that the life of Jesus may also be displayed in our bodies.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 4:11"/>
    For we who live are constantly being handed over to death for the sake of Jesus, so that His life may also be revealed in our mortal flesh.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 4:12"/>
    So then, death is at work in us, but life is at work in you.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Spirit of Faith</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 4:13"/>
    But having the same Spirit of faith, in accordance with what is written, “I believed, therefore I spoke,”* we also believe, and for that reason we also speak,
    <verse eid="2CO 4:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 4:14"/>
    knowing that the One who raised the Lord Jesus will also raise us with Jesus and will present us together with you.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 4:15"/>
    For all these things are for your benefit, so that grace, spreading to an ever-increasing number of people, may cause thanksgiving to overflow to the glory of God.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 4:16"/>
    Therefore, we do not lose heart. Even though our outer man is wasting away, yet our inner man is being renewed day by day.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 4:17"/>
    For our present affliction is light and momentary, yet it is producing for us an eternal weight of glory that surpasses all comparison,
    <verse eid="2CO 4:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 4:18"/>
    while we fix our attention not on what can be seen, but on what cannot be seen. For what is seen is temporary, but what is unseen is eternal.
    <verse eid="2CO 4:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">6 Quoted from Gen. 1:3</para>
  <para style="p">13 Quoted from Ps. 116:10</para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="2CO 5"/>
  <para style="s1">Our Eternal Building From God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 5:1"/>
    For we know with certainty that if our earthly dwelling, which is like a temporary tent, is torn down, we possess a permanent structure from God, a dwelling not made by human hands, eternal in the heavens.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 5:2"/>
    For while we live in this present condition, we groan inwardly, earnestly longing to be clothed with our heavenly dwelling,
    <verse eid="2CO 5:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 5:3"/>
    since when we are so clothed, we will not be found exposed or without covering.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 5:4"/>
    For while we remain in this earthly tent, we groan under its burden, not because we desire to be stripped of our present existence, but because we desire to be further clothed, so that what is mortal may be completely consumed by life.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 5:5"/>
    Now God Himself is the One who has prepared us for this very purpose and has given us the Spirit as a pledge and guarantee of what is to come.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 5:6"/>
    Therefore, we are always confident, knowing that while we are at home in the body, we are absent from the Lord—
    <verse eid="2CO 5:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 5:7"/>
    for we conduct our lives by faith, not by what is seen—
    <verse eid="2CO 5:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 5:8"/>
    yet we are confident and would rather prefer to be away from the body and to be at home with the Lord.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 5:9"/>
    For this reason, we make it our aim to please Him, whether we remain in the body or are away from it.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 5:10"/>
    For we must all appear before the judgment seat of Christ, so that each one may receive what is appropriate for what has been practised through the body, whether good or evil.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Ministry of Reconciliation</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 5:11"/>
    Therefore, knowing what it means to fear the Lord, we seek to persuade men, but our lives are fully known to God, and I hope they are also known in your consciences.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 5:12"/>
    We are not again promoting ourselves before you, but rather giving you an opportunity to take pride in us, so that you may have an answer for those who take pride in outward appearance rather than inward reality.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 5:13"/>
    For if we appear to be beside ourselves, it is for God; if we are of sound mind, it is for your benefit.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 5:14"/>
    For the love of Christ governs and directs us, because we have reached this settled conclusion: that One died on behalf of all, therefore all died.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 5:15"/>
    And He died for all so that those who live would no longer live for themselves, but for the One who died for them and was raised from the dead.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 5:16"/>
    Therefore, from this point forward, we regard no one merely from a human standpoint. Even though we once regarded Christ in this way, we no longer do so.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 5:17"/>
    Therefore, if anyone is in Christ, he belongs to a new creation. The former things have passed away; behold, new realities have come into being.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 5:18"/>
    Now all these things originate from God, who reconciled us to Himself through Christ and entrusted to us the ministry of reconciliation—
    <verse eid="2CO 5:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="2CO 5:19"/>
    namely, that God was acting in Christ to reconcile the world to Himself, not counting their trespasses against them, and He has entrusted to us the message of reconciliation.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="2CO 5:20"/>
    Therefore, we serve as representatives on behalf of Christ, as though God Himself were appealing through us. We plead with you on behalf of Christ: be reconciled to God.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="2CO 5:21"/>
    He made the One who knew no sin to be treated as sin for our sake, so that in Him we might become the righteousness that comes from God.
    <verse eid="2CO 5:21"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 5"/>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="2CO 6"/>
  <para style="s1">Encouragement Not to Receive God’s Grace in Vain</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 6:1"/>
    Now as those who labour together with God, we also urge you not to receive the grace of God in a fruitless way.
    <verse eid="2CO 6:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 6:2"/>
    For He says,
    <verse eid="2CO 6:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“In a favourable time I listened to you,</para>
  <para style="p">and in a day of salvation I came to your aid.”*</para>
  <para style="p">Look now, this is the favourable time;</para>
  <para style="p">look now, this is the day of salvation.</para>
  <para style="s1">The Experiences of the Apostles</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 6:3"/>
    We give no reason for anyone to stumble in any respect, so that the ministry will not be brought into disrepute,
    <verse eid="2CO 6:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 6:4"/>
    but in every circumstance we commend ourselves as servants of God: through great endurance, in afflictions, in hardships, in severe trials,
    <verse eid="2CO 6:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 6:5"/>
    in beatings, imprisonments, public disturbances, exhausting labor, sleepless nights, and hunger;
    <verse eid="2CO 6:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 6:6"/>
    in purity, knowledge, patience, kindness, in the Holy Spirit, in genuine love,
    <verse eid="2CO 6:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 6:7"/>
    in the word of truth, in the power of God, using the weapons of righteousness in the right hand and the left;
    <verse eid="2CO 6:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 6:8"/>
    through honour and dishonour, through slander and praise; regarded as deceivers, yet true, 
    <verse eid="2CO 6:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 6:9"/>
    as unknown, yet well known; as dying, yet see, we live; as punished, yet not put to death;
    <verse eid="2CO 6:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 6:10"/>
    as sorrowful, yet always rejoicing; as poor, yet making many rich; as having nothing, yet possessing everything.
    <verse eid="2CO 6:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 6:11"/>
    We have spoken openly to you, Corinthians; our heart has been opened wide.
    <verse eid="2CO 6:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 6:12"/>
    You are not restricted by us, but you are restricted in your own affections.
    <verse eid="2CO 6:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 6:13"/>
    Now in a corresponding response, I speak as to children: open your hearts wide also.
    <verse eid="2CO 6:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Against Unequal Yoking with Unbelievers</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 6:14"/>
    Do not be joined together in an unequal partnership with unbelievers. For what partnership exists between righteousness and lawlessness? Or what fellowship does light have with darkness?
    <verse eid="2CO 6:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 6:15"/>
    What harmony exists between Christ and Belial? Or what share does a believer have with an unbeliever?
    <verse eid="2CO 6:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 6:16"/>
    And what agreement does the temple of God have with idols? For we are the temple of the living God, just as God has said,
    <verse eid="2CO 6:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“I will dwell among them</para>
  <para style="p">and walk among them,</para>
  <para style="p">and I will be their God,</para>
  <para style="p">and they will be My people.*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 6:17"/>
    Therefore,
    <verse eid="2CO 6:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Come out from among them</para>
  <para style="p">and be separate, says the Lord,</para>
  <para style="p">and touch nothing unclean,</para>
  <para style="p">and I will welcome you,*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 6:18"/>
    and I will be a Father to you,
    <verse eid="2CO 6:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and you will be My sons and daughters,</para>
  <para style="p">says the Lord Almighty.”*</para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">2 Quoted from Is. 49:8</para>
  <para style="p">16 Quoted from Lev. 26:12. See also Jer. 32:38; Ezek. 37:27</para>
  <para style="p">17 Quoted from Is. 52:11</para>
  <para style="p">18 Rephrased from 2 Sam. 7:14; Is. 43:6</para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 6"/>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="2CO 7"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 7:1"/>
    Therefore, since these promises belong to us, beloved, let us purify ourselves from every form of defilement, both bodily and spiritual, bringing holiness to completion in reverent fear before God.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Paul’s Joy Over Genuine Repentance</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 7:2"/>
    Make room for us in your hearts. We have wronged no one, corrupted no one, and taken advantage of no one.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 7:3"/>
    I am not saying this to accuse you, for I have already said that you are so deeply in our hearts that we share life and death together.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 7:4"/>
    Great is my confidence in speaking openly to you, and great is my pride in you. I am filled with encouragement; in the midst of all our affliction, my joy overflows beyond measure.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 7:5"/>
    For even when we came into Macedonia, our bodies found no rest. Instead, we were afflicted on every side, with conflicts on the outside and fears within.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 7:6"/>
    But God, who comforts the downcast, encouraged us by the arrival of Titus,
    <verse eid="2CO 7:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 7:7"/>
    and not only by his arrival, but also by the encouragement he received from you. He reported to us your deep concern, your sorrow, and your zeal on my behalf, so that my joy increased all the more.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 7:8"/>
    For even if my letter caused you sorrow, I do not regret it. Though I did regret it for a time, since I see that the letter caused you pain, even if only briefly,
    <verse eid="2CO 7:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 7:9"/>
    I now rejoice, not because you were distressed, but because your distress led to repentance. You were grieved in a way that accorded with the purpose of God, so that you suffered no harm from us in any respect.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 7:10"/>
    For sorrow that accords with the purpose of God produces repentance that leads to salvation and leaves no regret, but worldly sorrow produces death.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 7:11"/>
    For consider what this very sorrow in accordance with God’s purpose has produced in you: such determination to clear yourselves, such righteous indignation, such reverent fear, such longing, such zeal, such readiness to see justice done. In every respect, you have shown yourselves to be innocent in this matter.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 7:12"/>
    Therefore, even though I wrote to you, it was not primarily for the sake of the one who committed the wrong, nor for the one who suffered it, but so that your earnest devotion to us might be made evident to you in the sight of God.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 7:13"/>
    For this reason, we have been encouraged. And beyond this encouragement, we rejoiced even more at the joy of Titus, because his spirit has been refreshed by all of you.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 7:14"/>
    For if I have spoken proudly to him about you, I was not put to shame. Just as everything we said to you was spoken truthfully, so our boasting to Titus about you proved to be true.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 7:15"/>
    And his affection for you has grown even deeper as he remembers the obedience of you all, how you welcomed him with reverence and humility.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 7:16"/>
    I rejoice because I have complete confidence in you.
    <verse eid="2CO 7:16"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 7"/>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="2CO 8"/>
  <para style="s1">The Grace of Generosity</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 8:1"/>
    Now we want you to know, brothers and sisters, about the grace of God that has been given among the churches of Macedonia,
    <verse eid="2CO 8:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 8:2"/>
    that in a severe trial of affliction, their abundant joy and their deep poverty overflowed into a wealth of generosity.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 8:3"/>
    For I testify that according to their means, and even beyond their means, they gave voluntarily,
    <verse eid="2CO 8:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 8:4"/>
    earnestly pleading with us for the privilege of sharing in this service to the saints.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 8:5"/>
    And they did this not merely as we had expected, but they first gave themselves to the Lord, and then to us, in keeping with the will of God.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 8:6"/>
    Accordingly, we urged Titus that just as he had begun this work earlier, so he would also bring this act of grace to completion among you.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 8:7"/>
    But just as you excel in everything—in faith, in speech, in knowledge, in all diligence, and in the love awakened among you—see that you also excel in this act of grace.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 8:8"/>
    I am not speaking this as a command, but as a means of testing the sincerity of your love through the earnestness of others.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 8:9"/>
    For you know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ: though He was rich, possessing all the glory and privileges of divinity, yet for your sake He became poor, willingly laying them aside to take on human flesh with its limitations and sufferings, so that through His poverty you might become rich—gaining the true riches of redemption and eternal life.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 8:10"/>
    And in this matter I offer my judgment, for this is beneficial for you, since you were the first not only to act but also to desire to do so a year ago.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 8:11"/>
    Now bring this work to completion as well, so that just as there was readiness to desire it, there may also be completion according to what you have.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 8:12"/>
    For if the willingness is present, the gift is acceptable according to what one has, not according to what one does not have.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 8:13"/>
    The goal is not that others should be relieved while you are burdened, but that there should be equality.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 8:14"/>
    At the present time, your abundance is meant to supply their need, so that their abundance may also supply your need, resulting in equality.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 8:15"/>
    As it is written, “The one who gathered much did not have too much, and the one who gathered little did not have too little.”*
    <verse eid="2CO 8:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Commendation of Titus</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 8:16"/>
    But thanks be to God, who has placed the same earnest concern for you in the heart of Titus.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 8:17"/>
    For he not only welcomed our appeal, but being himself very eager, he went to you of his own accord.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 8:18"/>
    We have also sent with him the brother whose commendation in the gospel is well known throughout all the churches.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="2CO 8:19"/>
    Not only that, but he has also been appointed by the churches to travel with us in administering this gracious gift, which we are managing for the glory of the Lord Himself and as an expression of our readiness to serve.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="2CO 8:20"/>
    We are taking precautions so that no one will criticise us regarding the administration of this generous gift.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="2CO 8:21"/>
    For we aim to do what is right, not only in the sight of the Lord, but also in the sight of men.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="2CO 8:22"/>
    Along with them, we have sent our brother whom we have often tested and found to be earnest in many matters, but now even more so because of his great confidence in you.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="2CO 8:23"/>
    If there is any question about Titus, he is my partner and fellow worker for your benefit. As for our brothers, they are messengers of the churches and a glory to Christ.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="2CO 8:24"/>
    Therefore, in the presence of the churches, show them the proof of your love and the reason for our confidence in you.
    <verse eid="2CO 8:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">15 Quoted from Ex. 16:18</para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 8"/>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="2CO 9"/>
  <para style="s1">The Service of Giving to the Poor Saints in Jerusalem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 9:1"/>
    It is really unnecessary for me to write further to you about this service for the saints,
    <verse eid="2CO 9:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 9:2"/>
    for I know your willingness, about which I boast of you to the Macedonians, saying that Achaia has been prepared since last year, and your zeal has stirred up most of them.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 9:3"/>
    Yet I have sent the brothers so that our confidence in you will not prove empty in this matter, and so that you may indeed be prepared, just as I have been saying.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 9:4"/>
    Otherwise, if any Macedonians come with me and find you unprepared, we—not to mention you—would be put to shame in this confident expectation.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 9:5"/>
    For this reason, I considered it necessary to urge the brothers to go ahead of us to you and make arrangements in advance for your previously promised generous gift, so that it would be ready as a gift freely given and not as something forced.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 9:6"/>
    Now this is the principle: The one who sows sparingly will also reap sparingly, and the one who sows generously will also reap generously.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 9:7"/>
    Each person must give as he has determined in his heart, not reluctantly or under compulsion, for God delights in a giver who gives with joy.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 9:8"/>
    And God is able to make all grace overflow to you, so that in every circumstance, having complete sufficiency at all times, you may abound in every good work.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 9:9"/>
    Just as it is written:
    <verse eid="2CO 9:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“He has scattered abroad,</para>
  <para style="p">He has given to the poor;</para>
  <para style="p">His righteousness endures forever.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 9:10"/>
    Now the One who supplies seed to the sower and bread for food will also supply and multiply your seed for sowing and increase the harvest that comes from your righteousness.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 9:11"/>
    In this way, you will be enriched in every respect for all generosity, which through us results in thanksgiving to God.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 9:12"/>
    For this service of ministry not only meets the needs of the saints, but also overflows in many expressions of gratitude to God.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 9:13"/>
    Through the tested character of this service, they will glorify God because of the submission that flows from your confession of the gospel of Christ and because of the generosity you share with them and with everyone else.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 9:14"/>
    And as they pray for you, they express deep affection for you because of the surpassing grace of God that rests upon you.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 9:15"/>
    Thanks be to God for His indescribable gift.
    <verse eid="2CO 9:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">9 Quoted from Ps. 112:9</para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 9"/>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="2CO 10"/>
  <para style="s1">Paul’s Defence of His Apostolic Ministry</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 10:1"/>
    Now I, Paul myself, appeal to you by the meekness and gentleness of Christ—I who am said to be humble when face to face with you, but bold toward you when absent.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 10:2"/>
    I ask that when I am present, I will not need to exercise boldness with the confidence I intend to use against some who think that we live according to merely human standards.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 10:3"/>
    For although we live in the body, we do not conduct our warfare according to human means,
    <verse eid="2CO 10:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 10:4"/>
    because the weapons of our warfare are not merely human, but are powerful through God for the destruction of strongholds.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 10:5"/>
    We are tearing down arguments and every proud obstacle that rises up against the knowledge of God, and we are bringing every thought into captivity to obey Christ.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 10:6"/>
    We are also prepared to deal with every act of disobedience, once your obedience is complete.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 10:7"/>
    You are judging by outward appearance. If anyone is convinced that he belongs to Christ, let him consider again that just as he belongs to Christ, so do we.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 10:8"/>
    For even if I boast somewhat freely about the authority the Lord gave us for building you up rather than tearing you down, I will not be put to shame.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 10:9"/>
    I do not want to seem as though I am trying to frighten you by means of my letters.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 10:10"/>
    For some say, “His letters are weighty and forceful, but his physical presence is unimpressive and his speech is disregarded.”
    <verse eid="2CO 10:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 10:11"/>
    Let such a person understand that what we are in our letters when absent, we will also be in our actions when present.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 10:12"/>
    For we do not dare to classify or compare ourselves with those who commend themselves. When they measure themselves by themselves and compare themselves with themselves, they show a lack of understanding.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 10:13"/>
    But we will not boast beyond proper limits. Instead, we will boast according to the measure of the sphere of ministry that God has assigned to us, which includes even you.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 10:14"/>
    For we are not overreaching, as though we had not come to you, since we did in fact come to you with the gospel of Christ.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 10:15"/>
    We are not boasting beyond proper limits in the labours of others. Rather, we have the hope that as your faith grows, our sphere of ministry among you will be greatly expanded within the boundaries God has assigned to us,
    <verse eid="2CO 10:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 10:16"/>
    so that we may proclaim the gospel in regions beyond you, without boasting in what has already been accomplished in someone else’s area of ministry.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 10:17"/>
    But “the one who boasts must boast in the Lord.”*
    <verse eid="2CO 10:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 10:18"/>
    For it is not the one who commends himself who is approved, but the one whom the Lord commends.
    <verse eid="2CO 10:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">17 Quoted from Jer. 9:24</para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 10"/>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="2CO 11"/>
  <para style="s1">Paul and the False Apostles</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 11:1"/>
    I ask you to bear with me in a display of what may seem foolish—but in truth, you are already bearing with me.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 11:2"/>
    For I am intensely jealous for you, with the very jealousy of God, because I have betrothed you to one husband, that you might be presented as a pure virgin to Christ.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 11:3"/>
    Yet I am concerned that, just as the serpent deceived Eve through his cunning, your minds might be led astray from the simplicity and the purity that is in Christ.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 11:4"/>
    For if anyone comes preaching a Jesus different from the One we proclaimed, or a spirit you did not receive, or a gospel you did not accept, you tolerate it all too easily.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 11:5"/>
    I consider myself in no way inferior to these so-called “super-apostles.”
    <verse eid="2CO 11:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 11:6"/>
    Even if I am unskilled in speech, I am not lacking in knowledge; indeed, we have demonstrated this to you fully in every way.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 11:7"/>
    Did I commit a wrong by humbling myself so that you might be exalted, because I preached the gospel of God to you without charge?
    <verse eid="2CO 11:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 11:8"/>
    I accepted assistance from other churches—at their expense—so that I could serve you.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 11:9"/>
    And when I was present with you and in need, I did not burden anyone, because the brothers from Macedonia supplied my needs. In all things, I kept myself from being a burden to you, and I will continue to do so.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 11:10"/>
    As the truth of Christ is in me, this boasting of mine will not be silenced in the regions of Achaia.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 11:11"/>
    Why? Is it because I do not love you? God knows that I do!
    <verse eid="2CO 11:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 11:12"/>
    What I am doing, I will continue to do, in order to remove any opportunity from those who seek one, so that they may be shown to be no better than we are in what they boast about.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 11:13"/>
    Such individuals are false apostles; they are deceptive workers who deliberately present themselves as apostles of Christ.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 11:14"/>
    And this should not surprise anyone, since even Satan makes himself appear as an angel of light.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 11:15"/>
    So it is no remarkable thing if his agents also disguise themselves as ministers of righteousness; their final outcome will correspond to what they have done.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Apostolic Sufferings of Paul</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 11:16"/>
    Again I say, let no one consider me foolish. But if they do, then receive me as foolish, so that I may boast a little.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 11:17"/>
    What I say, I do not speak as the Lord commands, but in this confidence of foolish boasting.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 11:18"/>
    Since many boast according to human standards, I also will boast.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="2CO 11:19"/>
    For you, being wise, gladly tolerate fools.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="2CO 11:20"/>
    You endure it if someone enslaves you, devours you, exploits you, exalts himself, or strikes you in the face.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="2CO 11:21"/>
    I speak in shame: we have been weak.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">Yet in whatever anyone else dares to boast about—I speak in foolishness—I also dare to boast.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="2CO 11:22"/>
    Are they Hebrews? So am I. Are they Israelites? So am I. Are they Abraham’s offspring? So am I. Are they servants of Christ? I am even more so: in far greater labors, in more imprisonments, in beatings beyond measure, and in frequent dangers of death.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="2CO 11:23"/>
    Five times I received from the Jews the forty lashes minus one.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="2CO 11:25"/>
    Three times I was beaten with rods, once stoned, three times shipwrecked, and I spent a day and a night adrift at sea.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="2CO 11:26"/>
    I have been on many journeys, in dangers from rivers, from robbers, from my own countrymen, from Gentiles; in cities, in the wilderness, at sea; in dangers among false brothers.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="2CO 11:27"/>
    I have endured labour and hardship, through many sleepless nights, in hunger and thirst, often without food, in cold and exposure.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="2CO 11:28"/>
    Beyond all this, there is the daily pressure of concern for all the churches.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="2CO 11:29"/>
    Who is weak, and I am not weak? Who falls into sin, and I do not burn with righteous indignation?
    <verse eid="2CO 11:29"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="2CO 11:30"/>
    If it is necessary to boast, I will boast about my weaknesses.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:30"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="2CO 11:31"/>
    The God and Father of the Lord Jesus, who is blessed forever, knows that I am not lying.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:31"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="2CO 11:32"/>
    In Damascus, the governor under King Aretas was guarding the city to seize me,
    <verse eid="2CO 11:32"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="2CO 11:33"/>
    but I was lowered in a basket through a window in the wall and escaped his hands.
    <verse eid="2CO 11:33"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 11"/>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="2CO 12"/>
  <para style="s1">Paul’s Visions and Revelations and His Thorn in the Flesh</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 12:1"/>
    I must continue boasting, though it brings no benefit or profit to me; yet I will proceed to speak of visions and revelations that the Lord has granted me.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 12:2"/>
    I know a man who belongs to Christ—this happened fourteen years ago—whether he was in his physical body or transported out of his body, I cannot say; only God knows the answer. This man was caught up and transported into the third heaven.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 12:3"/>
    And I know this same man—whether in his physical body or apart from his body, I do not know; God alone knows—
    <verse eid="2CO 12:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 12:4"/>
    that he was caught up into Paradise itself and heard words so sacred and profound that they cannot be expressed in human language, words which no person is permitted to utter or repeat.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 12:5"/>
    Concerning this man and his experience, I will boast and glory; but concerning my own self, I will not boast, except to glory in the things that reveal my weaknesses and frailties.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 12:6"/>
    For even if I should choose to boast about such experiences, I would not be acting foolishly, because I would be telling the truth. But I refrain from doing so, so that no one will form an opinion of me that goes beyond what he actually observes in my conduct or hears directly from my teaching.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 12:7"/>
    And so that I would not become proud or exalt myself because of the extraordinary nature of these revelations, a thorn was embedded in my flesh—a messenger or agent of Satan sent to torment and buffet me—so that I would not lift myself up in pride.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 12:8"/>
    Concerning this affliction, I pleaded earnestly with the Lord on three separate occasions, asking that it might be removed from me.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 12:9"/>
    And He responded to me, saying, “My grace is all you need and is fully adequate for you, for My power reaches its full strength and is made complete in the midst of human weakness.” Therefore, with the greatest joy and eagerness, I will boast in my weaknesses and infirmities, so that the power of Christ may dwell upon me and make its home in me.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Paul’s Concern for the Corinthian Believers</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 12:11"/>
    I have become foolish, as compelled by you. I ought to have been commended by you. For I am in no way inferior to these “super-apostles,” even though I am nothing in myself.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 12:12"/>
    Indeed, the signs of a true apostle were manifested among you with all perseverance, in signs, wonders, and miracles.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 12:13"/>
    In what respect were you treated as inferior to the other churches, except that I did not burden you? Forgive me this oversight.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 12:14"/>
    Behold, I am ready to come to you for the third time, and I will not burden you, for I am not seeking your possessions but you. For children ought not to save up for their parents, but parents for their children.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 12:15"/>
    But I will gladly spend and be spent for your souls. If I love you more, am I to be loved less?
    <verse eid="2CO 12:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 12:16"/>
    Nevertheless, I did not burden you. Yet, being prudent, I caught you by deceit.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 12:17"/>
    I did not take advantage of you through any of those whom I sent, did I?
    <verse eid="2CO 12:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 12:18"/>
    I urged Titus to go, and I sent another brother with him. Titus did not exploit you, did he? Did we not walk in the same Spirit? Did we not follow the same steps?
    <verse eid="2CO 12:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="2CO 12:19"/>
    You have thought all along that we were defending ourselves to you. But we speak in Christ before God, and all things, beloved, are for your spiritual upbuilding.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="2CO 12:20"/>
    For I fear that, when I come, I may not find you such as I desire, and you may find me such as you do not desire—lest there be quarrelling, jealousy, fits of anger, rivalries, slanders, arrogance, and disorderly conduct.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="2CO 12:21"/>
    Lest, when I come again, my God may humble me before you, and I may mourn over many of those who have sinned previously and have not repented of the impurity, sexual immorality, and sensuality they have practised.
    <verse eid="2CO 12:21"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 12"/>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="2CO 13"/>
  <para style="s1">Final Warnings</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 13:1"/>
    This is the third time I am coming to you. As the Scriptures say, “Every matter must be confirmed by the testimony of two or three witnesses.”*
    <verse eid="2CO 13:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 13:2"/>
    I have told you before, and I am saying it again in advance—just as when I was present the second time, and now while I am absent—to those who have sinned previously and to all the rest, that if I come again, I will not show leniency.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 13:3"/>
    You are seeking proof that Christ, who is not weak toward you but powerful among you, is truly speaking through me.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 13:4"/>
    For He was crucified in weakness, yet He lives by the power of God. Likewise, we are weak in Him, yet we will live with Him by the power of God directed towards you.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 13:5"/>
    Examine yourselves to determine whether you are truly in the faith; test yourselves! Do you not know that Jesus Christ is in you—unless you are unapproved?
    <verse eid="2CO 13:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 13:6"/>
    But I trust that you will recognise that we are not unapproved.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 13:7"/>
    Now we pray to God that you will do nothing wrong—not so that we may appear approved, but so that you may do what is right, even if we appear unapproved.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 13:8"/>
    For we have no authority to act against the truth, but only in support of the truth.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 13:9"/>
    For we rejoice when we are weak, while you are strong; and this is our prayer: that you may reach perfection or maturity.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 13:10"/>
    That is why I am writing these things while I am absent, so that when I come, I may not need to deal harshly with you, according to the authority the Lord has given me—for building up, not tearing down.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Final Greetings</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 13:11"/>
    Finally, brothers, rejoice; strive for perfection or maturity; be comforted; be unified in mind; be at peace. And the God of love and of peace will be with you.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 13:12"/>
    Greet one another with a holy kiss.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 13:13"/>
    All the saints send greetings to you.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 13:14"/>
    May the grace of the Lord Jesus Christ, the love of God, and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit be with all of you.
    <verse eid="2CO 13:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">1 Quoted from Deut. 19:15; cf. Num. 35:30</para>
  <chapter eid="2CO 13"/>
</usx>
